# What ships in this directory, and under whose licence

This is the published copy of the "Around the World in 80 Days" globe, served at
https://crowintelligence.org/verne/. The page itself is CC BY-NC-SA 4.0 and the code that
generated it is MIT — but four things here came from somebody else, and one of them is
copyleft.

Each licence text sits beside the files it covers, which is why this directory carries a
NOTICE at all: a licence in another repository is a licence that did not travel.


## data/borders_1880.json — GPL-3.0

Derived from `geojson/world_1880.geojson` in **historical-basemaps** by **André Ourednik**
(https://github.com/aourednik/historical-basemaps), at commit
`62d8f1a03a71f2d3ff17f2d166f7553f256bce68`.

That repository carries a plain, unmodified GNU General Public License v3.0 and no
separate licence for the data. The file here is a modified version of that work:
coordinates rounded to one decimal place, rings re-wound where the source wound a hole as
an exterior, features the source did not name removed, and everything dissolved into a
single geometry.

**It is distributed under the GPL-3.0, not under the licence of the page around it.** The
full text is at https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.txt.

Whether copyleft in fact reaches a rounded, re-wound, feature-filtered extract of geometry
is a question of law, not of fact. It is recorded here rather than resolved.

The source's own README says of the whole collection:

> It is __work in progress__: verify the maps by comparison to other sources before using
> in academic work.


## data/land.json and data/borders_modern.json — public domain

Derived from **Natural Earth** (https://www.naturalearthdata.com/), release `v5.1.2`,
files `ne_110m_land.geojson` and `ne_110m_admin_0_countries.geojson`. Natural Earth is
public domain: *"No permission is needed to use Natural Earth. Crediting the authors is
unnecessary."* The credit is given anyway.


## fonts/ — SIL Open Font License 1.1

Abril Fatface (Type-Ø-Tones), EB Garamond (Georg Duffner, Octavio Pardo) and Playfair
Display (Claus Eggers Sørensen), as subset woff2. The full licence text for each is in
this directory — `fonts/OFL-abrilfatface.txt`, `fonts/OFL-ebgaramond.txt`,
`fonts/OFL-playfairdisplay.txt` — because the OFL requires it to travel with the fonts.


## vendor/ — ISC

d3-geo, d3-array and internmap, by Mike Bostock. Full text in `vendor/LICENSES.md`, and
the versions and their hashes in `vendor/README.md`.


## The text the whole thing is about — public domain

*Around the World in Eighty Days* by Jules Verne, from Project Gutenberg ebook #103. The
chapter summaries and the extracted names are derived from it and are CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
along with the rest of the page.
